==English==
===Etymology===

Curator is originally Latin and means guardian or overseer.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}
# A person who [[manage]]s, [[administer]]s or [[organize]]s a [[collection]] - at a [[museum]], [[library]], [[archive]] or [[zoo]].

====Derived terms====
* [[curatorial]], [[curate]], [[curate|curated]]

